Subject: [PATCH] iommu/qcom: ignore disabled contexts when requesting secure tables

Disabled context banks are not populated as devices and cannot be used.
Do not allocate and transfer a secure page table to firmware solely because
such a context still exists in the DT. This lets a boot kernel use only the
non-secure display context without initializing unused camera/video secure
contexts, whose dynamic firmware-owned allocation lacks a kexec handoff.

diff --git a/drivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu/qcom_iommu.c b/drivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu/qcom_iommu.c
--- a/drivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu/qcom_iommu.c
+++ b/drivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu/qcom_iommu.c
@@ -761,7 +761,7 @@ static struct platform_driver qcom_iommu_ctx_driver = {
 
 static bool qcom_iommu_has_secure_context(struct qcom_iommu_dev *qcom_iommu)
 {
-	for_each_child_of_node_scoped(qcom_iommu->dev->of_node, child) {
+	for_each_available_child_of_node_scoped(qcom_iommu->dev->of_node, child) {
 		if (of_device_is_compatible(child, "qcom,msm-iommu-v1-sec") ||
 		    of_device_is_compatible(child, "qcom,msm-iommu-v2-sec"))
 			return true;
